@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] certificate-publication-validation
Only a CA-verified, currently valid server certificate for the configured hostname
with its matching private key may replace the published proxy certificate.
Validation or issuance failure MUST preserve the previously published certificate.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] certificate-secret-diagnostics
DNS credentials, private keys and raw ACME/provider diagnostics MUST NOT enter
logs, process arguments or the Nix store. DNS-01 credentials MUST come from the
selected private credential file, without an ambient or instance-role fallback.
HTTP-01 MUST NOT load DNS credentials. Neither mode may emit challenge tokens.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] certificate-retry-and-reload
Publication MUST verify that the certificate is served or request a validated
HAProxy reload or initial start.
Publication MUST be retried independently of whether the next ACME run issues
another certificate. Reload MUST preserve active WebSocket connections.
The last validated certificate MUST be persisted before requesting a reload.
Proxy startup MUST revalidate that certificate and MAY use it when issuance or
publication fails; an expired, untrusted or missing cache MUST fail startup.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] certificate-runtime-listener-address
When the proxy address is runtime data, publication and HTTP-01 ingress MUST
read it from the proxy's validated environment, never from the publication
file, and MUST fail rather than probe or bind a wildcard address.
